WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.960
Where's the head. Gary?
Someone's been down there. Gary.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Anything on the soil
in McGee's ute?

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.056
That's at the bottom
of my list.

4
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.480
Jonas McGee.
He was strangled to death.

5
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.080
The beheading... Came after.

6
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.520
I don't know where
Jonas was getting his black from.

7
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.560
but it was definitely not
down that mine.

8
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.640
So this is Kalingra.
Nobody works here.

9
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.920
That woman was
in Robbie Inglis's car.

10
00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.520
It was like she was a different
person. but that's her.

11
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.800
Get her on the hook.
She's so close.

12
00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.960
I can feel it.

13
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.440
You buried him
because he had what you wanted.

14
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.576
And eunuchs who have
made themselves so for the sake

15
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.200
of the kingdom of heaven.

16
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.880
You do me a favour.

17
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.680
Next time you talk to Phelan.
why don't you tell him I said hello?

18
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.200
Destroying key evidence
in a murder investigation.

19
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.040
Patricia. Patricia.
You're playing with fire.

20
00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.840
And now for tonight's
headline act.

21
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.880
A man who always reads the room just
a little too late.

22
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.440
A man who trusts first
and thinks second.

23
00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.080
Ooh!

24
00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.880
Your favourite lone ranger.

25
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:23.920
Detective Ivan Lucic!

26
00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.520
But tonight he's met his match.

27
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.520
She'll stab you in the back
and smile while she does it.

28
00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.480
Please welcome
Detective Nell Buchanan.

29
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.400
Where is my phone?

30
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.840
Ivan. are you OK?

31
00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.680
Oh.

32
00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.320
Did you lose your special
coin again?

33
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.160
Oh.

34
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.320
Did you lose your special boy again?

35
00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.560
Shut up. Dazzler!

36
00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.560
The mayor's dead.

37
00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.240
He's gone.

38
00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.120
-How long was he in the tub?
-Five. maybe six hours.

39
00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.800
Yeah. we had to fish him out.

40
00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.720
He was looking like a steamed
dim sim.

41
00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.440
That's lunch ruined.

42
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.016
All right. well. I'll get him back
to the morgue. do the autopsy.

43
00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.016
Gary. can you take Frank
for some fresh air?

44
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.720
Yes. sir. Yes. sir.
Three bags full. sir.

45
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.440
Detectives.

46
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.440
Please.

47
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.880
Sit.

48
00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.560
Thank you for coming.

49
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.960
What a way to go. eh?

50
00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.040
He loved that spa.

51
00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.520
It was his safe place.

52
00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.600
And yet...

53
00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.560
I told him not to keep the blender
so close.

54
00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.160
But...

55
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.120
..that was my Dougie.

56
00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.080
Always living life on the edge.

57
00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.640
Right. Pat?

58
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:26.680
Yeah.

59
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.640
Best ones always do.

60
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.680
Lydia. Mrs Mayor.

61
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.240
When was the last
time you saw your husband alive?

62
00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.760
It was after you left.

63
00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:51.880
I went to bed to get my beauty
sleep. and he decided to stay up.

64
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.760
He wanted to look at the stars.

65
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.440
Any other visitors?

66
00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.520
Detective. Please don't.

67
00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.840
This wasn't foul play. This...

68
00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.320
My husband was loved.

69
00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.240
This was a cruel accident.
Nothing else.

70
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.840
An accident.

71
00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.720
Darling.

72
00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.240
This town doesn't do subtle.
If someone wanted him dead.

73
00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.440
we'd know about it. wouldn't we.
Pat?

74
00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:37.320
Yeah.

75
00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:39.800
Yeah.

76
00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:43.840
Nice touch.

77
00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.280
The statue.

78
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.680
It's important for continuity.

79
00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.320
So this hasn't got anything to do
with your case.

80
00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.400
No?

81
00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.680
Why don't you just let the poor
woman grieve?

82
00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.400
Condolences.

83
00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.240
No foul play. my arse.

84
00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.520
Are you here for the
decapitation or the castration?

85
00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:45.720
Welcome to Nulla.
I'm the airport manager. Yuri Sidov.

86
00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.520
Detective Senior Sergeant Phelan.

87
00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.360
Is it always like this?
Oh. it gets worse in summer.

88
00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.040
This isn't summer.

89
00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.560
You're right.
Would you like some water?

90
00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.200
It's just $10.

91
00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.640
Does it hurt?

92
00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.560
Why would do you want to do
something like that?

93
00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.040
Put yourself in a place like this?

94
00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.080
I hate it here.

95
00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.160
It's not so bad.

96
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.480
I have a very good nurse.

97
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:36.560
What were you trying to prove?

98
00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.560
Was it...

99
00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.880
Was it a test or something?

100
00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:45.920
Hm?

101
00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.680
They need to see proof of my
devotion.

102
00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.856
If I didn't have my phone on me.

103
00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.120
David. you would have bled out.
Mum!

104
00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:53.400
He's resting.

105
00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.960
Your life isn't just yours anymore.

106
00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.400
Ivan. I can explain the Phelan
thing if you just let me.

107
00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.760
No? OK.

108
00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:24.240
Then can you at least tell me
why we're back where we started?

109
00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.320
We're missing something.

110
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.800
I guess I'll just go over here
and look for the thing we missed.

111
00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.560
Maybe we should try asking the bats
who killed Jonas.

112
00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:25.960
Maybe they saw something.

113
00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.760
We could just sit in the dark
and you could not tell me

114
00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.600
what we missed...

115
00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.040
or what you're thinking

116
00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:42.080
or why you would point a gun
at your own head.

117
00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.120
Is that what this is about?

118
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.240
Are we down here
so you can scare me some more?

119
00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:57.200
Oh. look. Some dirt.
Is that what we're looking for?

120
00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:02.360
Are we looking for dirt?
Because I can see a lot of it.

121
00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:06.880
No opal here.

122
00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:08.880
What!?

123
00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.480
Ivan!

124
00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:40.640
Through here.

125
00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.920
I think I'm in Ada's place.

126
00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.760
I think they're connected.

127
00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:22.800
Turn that off.

128
00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:48.480
What if it wasn't Jonas's opal?

129
00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.200
What if he was stealing it?

130
00:11:58.280 --> 00:11:59.600
From his sister.

131
00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.600
What now?

132
00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.280
Step outside. Ada.

133
00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:55.240
Why didn't you tell us there's
a crawl space?

134
00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:56.880
'Cause I don't know anything
about that.

135
00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.640
Yeah.

136
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.800
Ada Torshack. you're under arrest
for obstruction of justice...

137
00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.560
and under suspicion
for the murder of Jonas McGee.

138
00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:11.000
Well. I'd better lock up. then.

139
00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.080
Ada.

140
00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:37.360
No. no. no. no. no.

141
00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.200
Shit.

142
00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.400
How can we help you. Robbie?

143
00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.520
Did you hear the news?

144
00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:16.640
May he rest in peace. What?

145
00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:22.720
Kalingra went public.
Oh. it was a thing of bloody beauty.

146
00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:26.680
Our beige whale finally breached.
unlocked the whole deal.

147
00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:27.720
Breached?

148
00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.880
Yeah. We got a backdoor entry onto
the NASDAQ. Detective.

149
00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:32.816
The market's just closed.
I've been up all night.

150
00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:35.000
Who was your beige whale?
Your investors from China?

151
00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.720
No. Sadly. they fell through.

152
00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.760
Oh. did they find other acting work?

153
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:44.120
Ah! Here she is!

154
00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.760
Old moneybags herself.

155
00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:47.960
Hi. auntie!

156
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.320
This is your beige whale?

157
00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:58.200
Hey. Auntie Coll. Congratulations.
I knew you'd come around.

158
00:14:58.240 --> 00:14:59.400
Maybe you can use the money

159
00:14:59.440 --> 00:15:02.600
to turn those shit-catchers
into some grown-up pants.

160
00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:04.520
See you at the iron ring.

161
00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:08.400
Indeed. Indeed! Ah!

162
00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.760
There's a memorial going on
for the sun burnt whale.

163
00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.440
You know. Mayor Dougie.
May he rest in peace.

164
00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:17.120
So you're done with Kalingra?

165
00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.896
No. I've got a small parcel
under Founders Lock.

166
00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:20.320
but I can just sit back now.

167
00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:23.240
relax and watch Colleen dig herself
a big hole.

168
00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:29.000
Oh. did you guys catch the killer?
Nice. Good work.

169
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.800
So I might head off and try
and get some sleep.

170
00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.880
Any tips. Detective?

171
00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:36.960
Just kidding.

172
00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:44.640
Wanker.

173
00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:45.680
Ada.

174
00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:50.040
Not you. Him.

175
00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.400
Also you.

176
00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:53.440
Ada!

177
00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:57.720
Kyle. you're on speaker.
You gotta let my mum go.

178
00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.520
Kyle. stop!
Mum. you didn't do it.

179
00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.920
Kyle! I did it.

180
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.040
I cut his head off.

181
00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.040
Go! Drive!

182
00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.400
Kyle...

183
00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:50.400
you told us that Jonas was already
dead when you found him in the mine.

184
00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.480
Yeah.

185
00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:54.920
Yep.

186
00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.240
And his head was attached
when you found him.

187
00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:01.440
I...

188
00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:07.040
I went down there
to catch him ratting from us.

189
00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:10.080
I used the hole he dug.

190
00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:14.400
But he was just lying there dead.

191
00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.200
Head on.

192
00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.240
Mm.

193
00:17:21.320 --> 00:17:22.320
And then what happened?

194
00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.680
I knew... I knew it was David
who did it.

195
00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.280
I told you I heard them arguing
in Uncle Jonas's caravan.

196
00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:34.320
Mm-hm.

197
00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.800
He was threatening to expose David
for covering up Zig's death.

198
00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:45.360
He wanted hush money for Elsie
and Bess for their medical bills.

199
00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.720
I knew it was David who...
who'd shut him up.

200
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.600
and I knew he'd find a way
to get out of it too. you know.

201
00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.120
I couldn't let him do that.

202
00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.760
So I picked up the axe. and I...

203
00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.800
and... and I cut his head off.

204
00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:07.680
So you tried
to point us at David. right. Kyle?

205
00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:10.200
With the head.

206
00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.560
Matthew 11. verse 3.

207
00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.480
Yeah. Mm-hm.

208
00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:18.680
Yeah. like John the Baptist.
John the Baptist. Yeah.

209
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:25.640
Making someone look guilty isn't
the same as proving it. Kyle.

210
00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.360
That's why you're in here
and David's not.

211
00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:37.280
OK. Kyle. I have something
to show you.

212
00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.400
These are your phone records.

213
00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:44.920
See this one?

214
00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:49.920
Last Friday. just after you were
released from the station here...

215
00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:53.960
your first call was to your mum.

216
00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:00.120
Ada's admitted to us
what you said to her on the phone.

217
00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:05.720
But we'd like to hear
what she said to you.

218
00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:07.080
Now. please. Kyle.

219
00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.280
She...

220
00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:15.360
She said no-one would ever believe

221
00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:19.320
that I just walked in on him dead.

222
00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:21.320
And she said...

223
00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:22.400
She said...

224
00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:25.600
She said I'd be the one to go
down for it. not David.

225
00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.640
Mm-hm.

226
00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:30.600
So she fixed it.

227
00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:41.200
I need you to tell me how.
How did she fix it?

228
00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.720
How did she fix it. Kyle?

229
00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.240
She took the head...

230
00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:59.760
to pin it on someone else
and buy us...

231
00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:03.920
buy us some time
and make the trail messy.

232
00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:08.520
OK. So when was
the last time you saw Jonas alive?

233
00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.800
He came to see me.
I work at Kalingra.

234
00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:16.920
I thought he was going to apologise
for being a rat.

235
00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:18.880
but he was just sniffing around
for dirt.

236
00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:22.160
But I didn't kill him.

237
00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.240
That counts for something. yeah?

238
00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:28.320
Oh. Kyle.

239
00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:33.400
What you've done. Kyle.

240
00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.880
is you've altered human remains

241
00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:41.840
to pervert.
to manipulate the course of justice.

242
00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:44.360
Yeah.

243
00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.280
15 years. Kyle.

244
00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:53.040
15 years
for butchering your uncle's body.

245
00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.520
And for what?

246
00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.160
We still don't know who killed him.

247
00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:03.640
Sergeant.

248
00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.720
Kyle. you come with me. please.

249
00:21:23.600 --> 00:21:24.600
Take a seat. Luc.

250
00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:26.840
Shouldn't take long.

251
00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.080
Need you as a witness. Buchanan.

252
00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.320
Fuck!

253
00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:54.600
Carole?

254
00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:57.160
Nell. bad news. The
results came back on the soil sample

255
00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:59.560
that you found in McGee's ute.

256
00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:00.920
What have we got?

257
00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:03.800
Well. in layman's terms.
it's just regular dirt.

258
00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.496
The same dirt
I pulled off McGee's clothes.

259
00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:07.016
The man was practically marinated
in it.

260
00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:09.560
But. yeah. it's. uh...
It's just dirt. I'm sorry.

261
00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:11.640
Clothing.

262
00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:17.920
He came to see me.
I work at Kalingra.

263
00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:20.960
But he was just sniffing around
for dirt.

264
00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:25.760
Dirt.

265
00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:29.520
OK.

266
00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:37.960
Nell?

267
00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:15.440
Hey. pal.

268
00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:21.720
I see you've found yourself a pet.

269
00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:24.160
Well.
the opportunity presented itself.

270
00:23:25.240 --> 00:23:27.840
Like you with Goran Horvat. Hm.

271
00:23:31.280 --> 00:23:34.440
My senior partner
came clean with me

272
00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:37.480
about avenging the death of his son.

273
00:23:38.880 --> 00:23:42.400
It's great work.
Detective. Thank you.

274
00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:45.960
That's not what I said.
You're here as a witness. Buchanan.

275
00:23:47.000 --> 00:23:50.880
This is a ticket stub
to the Pooraka soccer club match

276
00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:52.680
just over 12 months ago.

277
00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:55.680
where Goran Horvat was executed
in the car park.

278
00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:59.720
It proves that you and Horvat were
in the same place at the same time.

279
00:23:59.760 --> 00:24:01.560
This is how we're doing it.

280
00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:07.120
It was found in the inside pocket
of this jacket in your apartment.

281
00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:08.520
Inadmissible.

282
00:24:08.560 --> 00:24:10.920
Forensics have tested it
for gunshot residue.

283
00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:13.520
Where's their report?
Yeah. I think I'd wash it.

284
00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:16.400
Why wasn't the stub damaged?
It was in your hand.

285
00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:18.000
and you put your hand in my pocket

286
00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:20.400
when you went into my home without
a warrant.

287
00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:23.360
Someone reported an animal
in distress.

288
00:24:23.400 --> 00:24:25.520
Very sloppy. Nathan.

289
00:24:27.000 --> 00:24:28.840
Very. very...

290
00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:30.920
sloppy.

291
00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:40.760
You lost your boy.

292
00:24:42.800 --> 00:24:43.840
I get it.

293
00:24:45.880 --> 00:24:47.120
I got two of my own now.

294
00:24:49.320 --> 00:24:53.200
If anything ever happened
to them on my watch...

295
00:24:57.720 --> 00:24:58.760
I couldn't...

296
00:25:03.240 --> 00:25:04.440
And all this...

297
00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:10.160
because your old man
killed Horvat's old man in Bukova?

298
00:25:11.920 --> 00:25:15.400
Father to son. Father to son.

299
00:25:15.440 --> 00:25:16.800
Father to son.

300
00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:19.880
So it goes.

301
00:25:24.360 --> 00:25:25.400
But it's Natalie...

302
00:25:28.160 --> 00:25:29.440
that I feel sorry for.

303
00:25:34.680 --> 00:25:38.080
I mean.
how could she possibly understand

304
00:25:38.120 --> 00:25:40.880
the family
that she was marrying into?

305
00:25:43.680 --> 00:25:46.000
Naturally. you'd blame yourself.

306
00:25:46.040 --> 00:25:48.560
I mean. you lost everything.

307
00:25:48.600 --> 00:25:51.240
You got pushed too far.
People understand that.

308
00:25:53.760 --> 00:25:55.080
But the law is the law.

309
00:25:59.160 --> 00:26:00.200
You're suspended.

310
00:26:01.240 --> 00:26:03.160
Effective immediately.

311
00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:06.960
pending an internal investigation
into the murder of Goran Horvat.

312
00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:11.760
Ivan.

313
00:26:13.280 --> 00:26:18.120
Gun and badge. Detective.

314
00:26:18.160 --> 00:26:20.200
I d... I didn't... Ivan...

315
00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:21.280
Ivan!

316
00:26:21.320 --> 00:26:22.320
Buchanan.

317
00:26:24.040 --> 00:26:26.720
PolAir leaves first thing
in the morning.

318
00:26:26.760 --> 00:26:30.680
You'll be waiting on that tarmac
or I'll bring you back in cuffs.

319
00:27:32.400 --> 00:27:35.800
Don't hang up. Ivan. listen to me.

320
00:27:35.840 --> 00:27:38.560
I didn't...
Phelan messed with that recording.

321
00:27:40.080 --> 00:27:41.200
You're a bad liar.

322
00:27:44.880 --> 00:27:47.480
You know I can hear you through
the walls.

323
00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:48.760
What?

324
00:27:48.800 --> 00:27:50.720
Through the walls.
I can hear you talking to him

325
00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:51.800
through the walls.

326
00:27:54.440 --> 00:27:55.880
On the phone? Yes.

327
00:27:57.040 --> 00:27:59.480
Oh. fuck. Ivan.
I'm not talking to Phelan.

328
00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:05.360
Then who are you talking to?

329
00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:07.240
Because you told me
that you have no-one.

330
00:28:13.160 --> 00:28:15.360
I talk to a fake woman on
the phone.

331
00:28:17.480 --> 00:28:18.520
There's this company

332
00:28:18.560 --> 00:28:21.440
that designs software
that sounds like human voices.

333
00:28:21.480 --> 00:28:27.480
and I speak to a fake voice
on the phone sometimes.

334
00:28:27.520 --> 00:28:30.560
She's for intimacy.

335
00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:34.640
This is why you called me? No.

336
00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:39.760
Then why did you call me?

337
00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:42.560
Because it's dirt. What?

338
00:28:42.600 --> 00:28:44.880
Kyle said the last time he saw Jonas.

339
00:28:44.920 --> 00:28:47.440
he was poking around Kalingra
for dirt.

340
00:28:47.480 --> 00:28:50.080
Then Carole calls me. says
the same thing.

341
00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:54.040
Says what?
The sample we found in McGee's ute.

342
00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:56.600
it's just dirt. OK.

343
00:28:56.640 --> 00:28:59.960
So why keep a tube of dirt
in your car?

344
00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.320
You're not keeping it.
You're testing it.

345
00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:04.480
Testing it for what?

346
00:29:06.280 --> 00:29:08.200
I don't know yet.

347
00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:09.280
I'm listening.

348
00:29:13.520 --> 00:29:14.600
Nell.

349
00:29:18.080 --> 00:29:20.120
Hello? Yes. Yes.

350
00:29:20.160 --> 00:29:21.360
Shit. I gotta go.

351
00:29:28.920 --> 00:29:30.440
Is this one of the mayor's drills.
Ray?

352
00:29:34.000 --> 00:29:36.640
This is private property.

353
00:29:38.960 --> 00:29:40.280
It's like he's still watching.

354
00:29:47.520 --> 00:29:48.560
What's the matter. Ray?

355
00:29:49.840 --> 00:29:50.920
You got something to hide?

356
00:29:52.600 --> 00:29:54.840
What are you up to. girlie?

357
00:29:54.880 --> 00:29:56.480
Nothin'.

358
00:29:56.520 --> 00:29:58.320
Do I have to run you out
of town again?

359
00:30:29.560 --> 00:30:32.000
What are you doing here?
I heard about David.

360
00:30:32.040 --> 00:30:34.400
Is he gonna make it?
Well. he has to.

361
00:30:34.440 --> 00:30:36.680
It's kind of a miracle. actually.
We just...

362
00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.080
Hospitals are weird.

363
00:30:45.160 --> 00:30:46.840
I can have a medevac on standby.

364
00:30:46.880 --> 00:30:48.096
take you all to Adelaide tonight.

365
00:30:48.120 --> 00:30:49.400
There are no strings.

366
00:30:49.440 --> 00:30:53.600
Why? Why-why are you here. Robbie?
Why?

367
00:30:53.640 --> 00:30:55.520
Because I like you. you weirdo.

368
00:30:56.760 --> 00:30:59.760
And because I want to help.
But why?

369
00:31:02.640 --> 00:31:05.680
Just be straight with me. OK?

370
00:31:05.720 --> 00:31:07.920
What makes you think I haven't
been straight with you?

371
00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.880
It's a feeling.

372
00:31:10.920 --> 00:31:13.280
Well. facts aren't feelings.
Elsie.

373
00:31:15.040 --> 00:31:17.000
Go on. Ask me anything you want.

374
00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:21.280
OK. What is your middle name?

375
00:31:21.320 --> 00:31:23.320
Lee. I was conceived in Lee's pub.

376
00:31:23.360 --> 00:31:24.760
OK. What was your first injury?

377
00:31:26.720 --> 00:31:30.640
I broke my arm jumping on
a trampoline.

378
00:31:30.680 --> 00:31:31.960
How did your dad die?

379
00:31:36.480 --> 00:31:38.440
It was a mining accident
at Cunnamulla.

380
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:44.320
He took a rock to the head
and he bled out in the dirt.

381
00:31:46.240 --> 00:31:47.280
He died alone.

382
00:31:49.240 --> 00:31:50.400
Oh. shit. Sorry.

383
00:31:52.440 --> 00:31:54.040
You asked.

384
00:31:54.080 --> 00:31:55.400
Yeah. and you answered.

385
00:31:58.320 --> 00:31:59.520
I have to go.

386
00:32:00.840 --> 00:32:03.880
I've got this tribute for the mayor.
I have to show up.

387
00:32:05.320 --> 00:32:09.640
Can I please find you after?
Not if I find you first.

388
00:32:09.680 --> 00:32:10.680
Mm...

389
00:32:12.080 --> 00:32:14.120
Yes. Come find me.

390
00:32:15.560 --> 00:32:16.600
Thank you.

391
00:32:35.520 --> 00:32:39.760
You've reached Detective Ivan Lucic.
I can't make it to the phone.

392
00:32:41.080 --> 00:32:43.400
Ivan. call me.
I'm following a lead.

393
00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:46.160
I know you're suspended. but I...

394
00:32:46.200 --> 00:32:47.960
I need... I...

395
00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:49.400
Just call me back. OK?

396
00:35:02.400 --> 00:35:03.400
Ray.

397
00:35:05.680 --> 00:35:07.960
Find what you were looking for?

398
00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:10.240
Oh-oh-oh.

399
00:35:10.280 --> 00:35:11.840
Now. before you delete that.

400
00:35:11.880 --> 00:35:13.320
put your hands up. Ray.

401
00:35:15.560 --> 00:35:20.320
It's cosy in here. isn't it?
The mayor's little laundry room.

402
00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:21.400
Give us a spin.

403
00:35:25.960 --> 00:35:30.160
I had a hunch about this place.
of course. but you did the rest.

404
00:35:30.200 --> 00:35:32.440
Thanks for that. Ray.
I appreciate it.

405
00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:35.720
Don't let me interrupt.

406
00:35:38.760 --> 00:35:39.880
Turn around.

407
00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:47.000
Let's have a look.

408
00:35:54.080 --> 00:35:55.840
Pull up Kalingra for me. Ray.

409
00:35:58.440 --> 00:35:59.800
Tuesday. please.

410
00:36:09.320 --> 00:36:10.320
Stop!

411
00:36:11.560 --> 00:36:12.920
There's McGee's ute.

412
00:36:19.400 --> 00:36:20.440
Hello. Jonas.

413
00:36:24.880 --> 00:36:26.720
What happened to you?

414
00:36:39.960 --> 00:36:44.200
You've reached Detective Ivan Lucic.
I can't make it to the phone.

415
00:36:45.280 --> 00:36:47.840
Ivan. pick up. I figured it out.
I know who did it.

416
00:36:47.880 --> 00:36:49.680
I have footage of the murder.

417
00:36:49.720 --> 00:36:52.800
I know who killed Jonas McGee.
I saw all of it.

418
00:36:52.840 --> 00:36:55.120
I saw all of it.
The mayor saw all of it. actually.

419
00:36:55.160 --> 00:36:56.720
I locked Ray in his basement.

420
00:36:56.760 --> 00:36:59.240
I left Ray watching footage
in his basement.

421
00:36:59.280 --> 00:37:01.240
which maybe wasn't smart.

422
00:37:01.280 --> 00:37:02.520
I don't have anyone else.

423
00:37:04.880 --> 00:37:06.360
So I need you to answer the phone.

424
00:37:10.840 --> 00:37:12.320
And I need you to still be here.

425
00:37:13.960 --> 00:37:16.720
Pick up the phone!

426
00:37:19.800 --> 00:37:20.840
Ivan!

427
00:37:25.120 --> 00:37:26.160
Ivan.

428
00:37:37.440 --> 00:37:38.640
That's not yours.

429
00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:13.440
What happened to your ears?
The mayor.

430
00:38:14.480 --> 00:38:15.480
Huh.

431
00:38:17.120 --> 00:38:18.120
Thought you were dead.

432
00:38:20.280 --> 00:38:22.000
No. Not yet anyway.

433
00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:31.680
The iron ring.

434
00:38:31.720 --> 00:38:33.400
The iron ring. Mm.

435
00:38:33.440 --> 00:38:35.040
Hm.

436
00:38:35.080 --> 00:38:36.840
I'm only the under card.

437
00:38:36.880 --> 00:38:38.280
But you're the main event. mate.

438
00:38:41.400 --> 00:38:43.120
Man Mountain. Hey.

439
00:38:49.520 --> 00:38:50.520
Hey...

440
00:38:53.120 --> 00:38:55.400
How's Nelly? Sorry - Nell.

441
00:38:55.440 --> 00:38:56.960
She's good.

442
00:38:57.000 --> 00:38:58.600
Is she?

443
00:39:00.040 --> 00:39:01.600
One minute!

444
00:39:08.920 --> 00:39:11.960
Mister. The Irishman.

445
00:39:12.000 --> 00:39:14.080
Did Jonas ever talk to you
about Kalingra?

446
00:39:14.120 --> 00:39:16.680
Eh?
Jonas. Talk to you about Kalingra?

447
00:39:16.720 --> 00:39:18.216
Look. I'm trying to concentrate
here. mate.

448
00:39:18.240 --> 00:39:19.920
Kalingra. Uh. yeah.

449
00:39:19.960 --> 00:39:21.840
He brought me a sample to test
for him.

450
00:39:21.880 --> 00:39:23.240
A soil sample? Yeah.

451
00:39:23.280 --> 00:39:24.480
Why did he bring it here?

452
00:39:24.520 --> 00:39:27.040
A geology minor
at the University of Aberdeen.

453
00:39:27.080 --> 00:39:29.280
Thank you very much.
He did? Wow.

454
00:39:29.320 --> 00:39:31.080
I didn't see that coming.

455
00:39:31.120 --> 00:39:32.680
Nope. What did you find?

456
00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:36.480
Uh... uh... uh... Igneous rock.
Uh. quartzite.

457
00:39:36.520 --> 00:39:38.480
Clay loam. Salt.

458
00:39:38.520 --> 00:39:41.080
No. uh. rare earth minerals?

459
00:39:41.120 --> 00:39:43.040
No. mate. Zero. Zero.

460
00:39:44.640 --> 00:39:45.720
Show time. Irish.

461
00:40:29.200 --> 00:40:31.200
Hey. Frank.

462
00:40:32.280 --> 00:40:33.320
No weapons.

463
00:40:35.240 --> 00:40:38.240
Mrs Mayor's rules.
Who's fighting?

464
00:40:49.120 --> 00:40:50.480
Behold...

465
00:40:52.280 --> 00:40:55.360
the counterfeiter who thought he
could cheat this town.

466
00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:13.120
One. two. three. four. five.

467
00:41:19.080 --> 00:41:24.040
Tonight we honour my husband
and his legacy.

468
00:41:24.080 --> 00:41:26.360
My Dougie built this place.

469
00:41:26.400 --> 00:41:28.000
But I'm gonna make it...

470
00:41:28.040 --> 00:41:29.960
LEGENDARY!

471
00:41:32.160 --> 00:41:36.560
Now how about a big iron ring
welcome

472
00:41:36.600 --> 00:41:39.120
to tonight's benefactors.

473
00:41:39.160 --> 00:41:43.520
Colleen Delaney and Robbie Inglis.

474
00:41:45.920 --> 00:41:47.840
You're just in time for the finale.

475
00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:54.400
Introducing a detective...

476
00:41:56.520 --> 00:41:58.120
Who gambled with
the wrong people...

477
00:42:00.440 --> 00:42:04.480
up against the undefeated
people's champion.

478
00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:11.440
Stan 'the Mountain Man' Honeywell!

479
00:42:16.200 --> 00:42:17.720
Ivan! Ivan.

480
00:42:19.160 --> 00:42:21.360
Nell. it's Robbie. Yes.

481
00:42:21.400 --> 00:42:24.720
I have footage of him killing Jonas
with CCTV.

482
00:42:24.760 --> 00:42:27.120
Go get him. They took my gun.

483
00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:33.680
I'll buy you some time. What?

484
00:42:33.720 --> 00:42:35.320
I'll buy you some time.

485
00:42:35.360 --> 00:42:36.960
What? In there?

486
00:42:38.440 --> 00:42:39.440
He'll kill you!

487
00:42:41.720 --> 00:42:44.320
Make it quick. I'll try.

488
00:42:44.360 --> 00:42:46.800
Place your bets!

489
00:42:55.120 --> 00:42:56.400
Fight!

490
00:43:02.040 --> 00:43:03.480
Stanley.

491
00:43:03.520 --> 00:43:07.000
Stanley. Hey. Listen. Listen to me.

492
00:43:07.040 --> 00:43:08.720
Ho!

493
00:43:08.760 --> 00:43:12.680
Hey. Stanley. Stanley. listen to me.
It's about Jonas.

494
00:43:16.000 --> 00:43:19.920
It's about Jonas. Your friend.
It's about your friend.

495
00:43:21.520 --> 00:43:22.560
Listen. listen.

496
00:43:28.600 --> 00:43:32.680
Well. cheers. Coll. To the future.

497
00:43:32.720 --> 00:43:34.240
You mean my future?

498
00:43:36.080 --> 00:43:40.800
I had my own geological surveys done
at Kalingra months ago.

499
00:43:41.960 --> 00:43:44.080
There are no rare earth minerals.

500
00:43:46.360 --> 00:43:47.640
But you already knew that.

501
00:43:49.360 --> 00:43:52.680
What there is is lithium.

502
00:43:52.720 --> 00:43:57.160
Trace amounts. Too small for
an amateur like you to notice.

503
00:43:57.200 --> 00:43:58.920
But you know what that means.
Robbie.

504
00:43:58.960 --> 00:44:00.880
Batteries.

505
00:44:00.920 --> 00:44:01.960
The future.

506
00:44:03.120 --> 00:44:05.240
So much effort to con me into buying

507
00:44:05.280 --> 00:44:07.960
what you thought was a worthless
patch of dirt.

508
00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:10.320
And you missed what was under it.

509
00:44:10.360 --> 00:44:12.560
Stanley. listen.

510
00:44:13.560 --> 00:44:18.000
I know who killed Jonas.
Robbie Inglis.

511
00:44:18.040 --> 00:44:19.080
Uh...

512
00:44:20.320 --> 00:44:23.440
Nice try
with your dirty little revenge play.

513
00:44:24.640 --> 00:44:26.360
You think your father would be proud
of you?

514
00:44:27.320 --> 00:44:30.680
I think he'd be glad he didn't
live to watch you fail him.

515
00:44:30.720 --> 00:44:32.160
Ah!

516
00:44:33.760 --> 00:44:35.320
Ah!

517
00:44:37.200 --> 00:44:39.800
Merv. get me out of this shithole.

518
00:44:52.040 --> 00:44:53.080
Stanley!

519
00:45:01.840 --> 00:45:02.880
Robbie!

520
00:45:07.680 --> 00:45:11.040
Robert Inglis. you're under arrest
for the murder of Jonas McGee.

521
00:45:12.960 --> 00:45:14.840
No back-up. You're brave.

522
00:45:32.400 --> 00:45:35.000
No. Stanley! Stanley. no!

523
00:45:36.520 --> 00:45:38.840
Stanley! Stanley. look at me!
Look at me.

524
00:45:38.880 --> 00:45:40.000
Let him go! No!

525
00:45:40.040 --> 00:45:41.920
Let go! No!

526
00:45:41.960 --> 00:45:44.320
Stanley. you will go back to us.

527
00:45:44.360 --> 00:45:46.696
You will go right back to prison.
I can't keep you out of prison.

528
00:45:46.720 --> 00:45:48.400
You're gonna kill him! Let him go!

529
00:45:52.520 --> 00:45:54.080
He killed my friend.

530
00:45:54.120 --> 00:45:56.040
I can arrest him. I can arrest him.

